# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7
# fabloom-verifier: the L0 image of the Sandboxes ladder (ADR-0003).
#   batfish/allinone (pinned by digest) + fabloom's verify plane + a baked JVM AOT cache.
# ConTree imports sandbox images from an OCI registry: if this image is not published to
# GHCR, sandboxes cannot run at all. Built and pushed by .github/workflows/ci.yml.

ARG BATFISH_IMAGE=batfish/allinone:2026.08.27.3685@sha256:54cb0ed94fd9a3c1ca0985f73e5be479e955cee9b9f6a6799b66be3364fd8e5c

# --- stage 1: build the fabloom wheel ------------------------------------------------------
FROM python:3.12-slim AS build
COPY --from=ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:0.11.24 /uv /bin/uv
WORKDIR /src
COPY pyproject.toml uv.lock README.md LICENSE NOTICE ./
COPY src ./src
RUN uv build --wheel --out-dir /dist

# --- stage 2: verifier ------------------------------------------------------------------
FROM ${BATFISH_IMAGE}
ARG GIT_SHA=unknown
ARG BAKE_AOT=1
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.source="https://github.com/vkrishnabhatk/fabloom" \
      org.opencontainers.image.licenses="Apache-2.0" \
      org.opencontainers.image.description="Batfish + fabloom-verify for Nebius Sandboxes"
# Close what the upstream image leaves open (Trivy, fixable HIGH/CRITICAL only):
# - Ubuntu packages with released fixes (kernel headers, openssl).
# - Jupyter: the base image's notebook server, which start-batfish.sh never starts. It is
#   removed rather than patched (nbconvert and nbclient too); pillow, tornado, urllib3 and certifi are upgraded because
#   pybatfish or the AOT training run may still import them.
# - /usr/bin/pebble: the Ubuntu base's service manager. The entrypoint is fabloom-verify,
#   so nothing runs it, and its Go stdlib findings cannot be fixed from here.
# What remains is listed, with a reason per finding, in .trivyignore.
RUN apt-get update \
 && DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get upgrade -y --no-install-recommends \
 && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* \
 && rm -f /usr/bin/pebble \
 && (pip3 uninstall -y --break-system-packages jupyterlab notebook jupyter_server nbconvert nbclient 2>/dev/null || true) \
 && pip3 install --break-system-packages --no-cache-dir --upgrade pillow tornado urllib3 certifi
# The verify plane needs only pydantic beyond what the base image has (pybatfish ships in it,
# version-matched to the server). --no-deps keeps the model-side dependencies out.
COPY --from=build /dist/*.whl /tmp/
RUN pip3 install --break-system-packages --no-cache-dir --no-deps /tmp/fabloom-*.whl \
 && pip3 install --break-system-packages --no-cache-dir "pydantic>=2.9,<3" \
 && rm /tmp/*.whl
COPY docker/verifier/start-batfish.sh docker/verifier/bake-aot.sh /opt/fabloom/
COPY docker/verifier/training/ /opt/fabloom/training/
RUN if [ "$BAKE_AOT" = "1" ]; then /opt/fabloom/bake-aot.sh; fi

RUN useradd --uid 10001 --no-create-home --home-dir /data fabloom \
 && chown -R fabloom /data
USER 10001
ENV IMAGE_TAG=${GIT_SHA} \
    FABLOOM_BATFISH_START_CMD=/opt/fabloom/start-batfish.sh
ENTRYPOINT ["fabloom-verify"]
